WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.839 --> 00:00:11.900
assembly was over.

2
00:00:13.201 --> 00:00:15.443
The campers walked across the square in the dark.

3
00:00:17.064 --> 00:00:21.167
Ivy, Glen, and Ezra were still talking about Ivy's idea to leave camp.

4
00:00:22.808 --> 00:00:24.950
Glen used his flashlight to light up the way.

5
00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.592
"I don't want to leave.

6
00:00:28.844 --> 00:00:32.006
This is the summer when everyone figures out how cool I am.

7
00:00:32.566 --> 00:00:35.988
Finally!" Ezra bit his lip.

8
00:00:36.008 --> 00:00:38.610
"I don't want to get in trouble.

9
00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:42.952
But I wouldn't mind leaving—I miss my parents.

10
00:00:43.953 --> 00:00:45.794
I've already written them two letters."

11
00:00:45.814 --> 00:00:49.536
"Well, I'm breaking out of here no matter what!"

12
00:00:50.136 --> 00:00:50.636
Ivy said.

13
00:00:50.656 --> 00:00:56.500
"If you want to come along, we can make plans tomorrow."

14
00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.822
The next morning the campers gathered in the lodge after breakfast.

15
00:01:07.302 --> 00:01:10.524
Private was checking each group's plans for the spirit contest.

16
00:01:12.585 --> 00:01:14.105
She walked over to Ivy's group.

17
00:01:15.306 --> 00:01:16.987
"State your idea, campers!"

18
00:01:18.527 --> 00:01:20.228
The kids looked at each other nervously.

19
00:01:20.248 --> 00:01:25.271
"We have a great idea," Glen said.

20
00:01:25.291 --> 00:01:28.292
"But we don't want the others stealing it!"

21
00:01:31.352 --> 00:01:33.153
Private jotted a note on her clipboard.

22
00:01:33.173 --> 00:01:38.056
"Got it—top secret," she said before walking away.

23
00:01:41.138 --> 00:01:41.818
Ivy grinned.

24
00:01:41.838 --> 00:01:46.180
"By the time the spirit contest happens, we'll be out of here!"

25
00:01:48.802 --> 00:01:52.224
Later that morning a counselor named Mango introduced himself.

26
00:01:53.745 --> 00:01:55.766
He was leading the campers on a nature walk.

27
00:01:57.227 --> 00:01:59.288
Mango peered through a pair of binoculars.

28
00:02:02.604 --> 00:02:05.386
"Today we'll be searching for the blue-footed warbler.

29
00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:08.608
It makes its nests in pine trees."

30
00:02:09.309 --> 00:02:09.889
He grinned.

31
00:02:09.909 --> 00:02:14.412
"It's also been known to nest in the soup pots in the mess hall.

32
00:02:15.733 --> 00:02:16.934
Follow me, everyone!"

33
00:02:18.755 --> 00:02:20.556
The kids walked along the hiking trail.

34
00:02:20.576 --> 00:02:24.359
"So," Ivy whispered.

35
00:02:24.379 --> 00:02:25.800
"How can we escape?

36
00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.461
There's a high fence around the whole camp."

37
00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:32.224
Ezra pulled some rolled-up toilet paper from his pocket.

38
00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.101
"My dad is good at building things.

39
00:02:35.702 --> 00:02:36.822
Sometimes I help him.

40
00:02:37.843 --> 00:02:39.544
Maybe we can build a catapult."

41
00:02:41.005 --> 00:02:43.487
Ezra unrolled the paper to show them his diagram.

42
00:02:43.507 --> 00:02:47.409
"We can cut down a small tree for the frame.

43
00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.913
Then we'll tie the boards together with old strands of spaghetti.

44
00:02:52.753 --> 00:02:55.035
I hear that's what we're having for lunch today."

45
00:02:56.756 --> 00:02:57.636
Ivy made a face.

46
00:02:57.656 --> 00:03:00.518
"Is the spaghetti that tough?"

47
00:03:01.699 --> 00:03:02.680
Both boys nodded.

48
00:03:03.972 --> 00:03:05.974
Ivy and Glen studied Ezra's drawing.

49
00:03:05.994 --> 00:03:09.396
"Looks good but where's the bucket?"

50
00:03:09.796 --> 00:03:10.417
Glen asked.

51
00:03:11.418 --> 00:03:14.600
"You know—the part we sit in that will launch us over the fence."

52
00:03:15.921 --> 00:03:17.582
Ezra shrugged and looked at his feet.

53
00:03:17.602 --> 00:03:20.324
"I didn't get that far.

54
00:03:21.925 --> 00:03:23.606
I ran out of toilet paper."

55
00:03:23.626 --> 00:03:26.408
"Hey, kids!"

56
00:03:26.829 --> 00:03:27.609
Mango shouted.

57
00:03:27.629 --> 00:03:31.472
"A rare four-toed salamander!"

58
00:03:32.872 --> 00:03:34.352
Everyone gathered around to look.

59
00:03:34.372 --> 00:03:39.974
"Salamanders are nearly extinct in these woods," Mango said.

60
00:03:40.874 --> 00:03:42.215
Chuck pointed under a log.

61
00:03:42.235 --> 00:03:43.575
"There's one."

62
00:03:44.695 --> 00:03:46.076
Huck held up a glass jar.

63
00:03:46.096 --> 00:03:48.476
"I caught three yesterday."

64
00:03:48.496 --> 00:03:52.818
"So exciting to see the salamanders making a comeback!"

65
00:03:53.638 --> 00:03:54.818
Mango sighed happily.

66
00:03:56.258 --> 00:03:57.599
The group continued their hike.

67
00:03:57.619 --> 00:04:01.580
"I've decided I'll escape with you," Glen whispered.

68
00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.762
"Years from now, campers will gather around the campfire.

69
00:04:07.083 --> 00:04:11.086
They'll tell stories about amazing Glen Brown's daring escape.

70
00:04:12.247 --> 00:04:14.088
I'll be a Camp Evergreen legend!"

71
00:04:14.108 --> 00:04:18.351
"Okay, amazing Glen," Ivy said.

72
00:04:18.371 --> 00:04:22.193
"Got any amazing ideas about how to break out of here?"

73
00:04:23.174 --> 00:04:23.875
Glen nodded.

74
00:04:23.895 --> 00:04:26.777
"We're surrounded by wild animals.

75
00:04:27.537 --> 00:04:29.138
Why don't we use their techniques?

76
00:04:30.379 --> 00:04:31.420
We can tunnel out!"

77
00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:34.340
"Let's stop here for a second!"

78
00:04:34.761 --> 00:04:35.921
Mango said suddenly.

79
00:04:37.781 --> 00:04:40.282
Ivy watched Mango crawl through a hole in the fence.

80
00:04:41.302 --> 00:04:42.983
He laid some carrots on the ground.

81
00:04:43.003 --> 00:04:51.565
"For my little opossum friends," Mango said, looking up into the trees with his binoculars.

82
00:04:52.446 --> 00:04:53.806
Ivy turned back to the boys.

83
00:04:54.666 --> 00:04:55.627
"Here's an idea.

84
00:04:56.987 --> 00:04:59.308
Why don't we just climb through that hole in the fence?"
